diff --git a/doc/unbound.conf.rst b/doc/unbound.conf.rst
index 74f242a..f656a8b 100644
--- a/doc/unbound.conf.rst
+++ b/doc/unbound.conf.rst
@@ -1489,6 +1489,32 @@ These options are part of the ``server:`` section.
     Set view for given access control element.
 
 
+@@UAHL@unbound.conf@mesh-isolate-client-tags@@: *<yes or no>*
+    If enabled, clients whose
+    :ref:`access-control<unbound.conf.access-control>` elements carry
+    different tags
+    (:ref:`access-control-tag<unbound.conf.access-control-tag>`) or views
+    (:ref:`access-control-view<unbound.conf.access-control-view>`) never
+    share an in-flight query state, for any query type.
+    Identical queries from clients with the same tags and view still share
+    one state.
+
+    By default, tags and views separate in-flight query states only for A,
+    AAAA and ANY queries, and only when response-ip or RPZ is configured.
+    Otherwise every client that asks the same question while it is being
+    resolved receives the answer computed for the first client.
+    That is wrong for modules that answer per client, such as a Python
+    module that applies client-specific policy in its operate function.
+    Tag such clients by policy and enable this option.
+
+    This option does not separate the message and RRset caches; a module
+    that produces client-specific answers must also avoid storing them.
+    It costs one copy of the tag list per query state and removes
+    coalescing between clients of different tags or views.
+
+    Default: no
+
+
 @@UAHL@unbound.conf@interface-action@@: *<ip address or interface name [@port]> <action>*
     Similar to :ref:`access-control<unbound.conf.access-control>` but for
     interfaces.
